  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Arcade Desktop",
    "overview": "Anki XP is a faithful Windows XP Luna desktop that hosts a loud little arcade. The frame is 2003 and taken seriously: Luna blue title bars with the light top edge and dark navy text shadow, beige window faces, white Explorer lists, push buttons with the white-to-beige gradient, message boxes with real XP icons, balloon tips, group boxes with their label set into the frame. Inside that calm frame, the reward moments are allowed to shout: gold \"+XP\" pops, cyan and coral combo chips, a fire-coloured combo counter, a boss card, 8-bit sounds. The contrast between the sober desktop and the bright arcade is the personality.\n\nIt is a phone app first. XP supplies the look; phone ergonomics supply the rules: touch targets, contrast measured against the scanlines, and Android Back all win over pixel-faithful XP when they conflict. Density is XP-normal (13-15sp Tahoma, tight 5-8dp gaps), never crammed below a usable target. A CRT scanline layer sits over every window, menu and dialog, in step across windows, and can be turned off.\n\nRejected outright: Material You shapes (pill toggles, M3 chips, tonal FABs, big rounded cards) and any other Windows era (98 grey, Vista/7 glass, 10/11 flat). If it does not look like it shipped with XP Luna, it does not belong.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Every screen is an XP object: window, message box, Explorer list, group box, Start menu, balloon tip.",
      "One selection colour (XP selection blue) marks every chosen, active or pressed-on state.",
      "Calm frame, loud rewards: saturated colour belongs to game moments, not to chrome.",
      "Tahoma everywhere, bold with a navy shadow on title bars.",
      "Small corners (3px controls, 8px window tops), 1px hard borders, no soft shadows on controls.",
      "CRT scanlines over everything, optional."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Selection Rule",
        "body": "Anything chosen, active or toggled on uses Selection Blue fill with white text. Never a pale tint alone, never a second \"selected\" colour.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Arcade Is Earned Rule",
        "body": "Gold, cyan, coral and fire colours appear only as feedback to a review answer. Chrome, settings and lists never use them.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tahoma Only Rule",
        "body": "Native and web surfaces use XP Tahoma; no Roboto, Inter or system fonts visible where Tahoma can load.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Hard Edge Rule",
        "body": "No blurred elevation on controls or cards. Depth is a gradient or a 1px line.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** build every new surface out of XP objects (window, group box, message box, Explorer list, balloon tip) before inventing anything.",
      "**Do** mark every chosen or active state with Selection Blue fill and white text.",
      "**Do** keep touch targets at 32dp+ for settings controls and 38dp+ for dialog buttons, even when real XP was smaller.",
      "**Do** check contrast on a scanline row (about #E1E1E1 on white, #C4C2B4 on the face), not on plain white.",
      "**Do** style backend web pages only through Anki's CSS variables and generic elements, and exclude Anki's small icon buttons (revert, help) from the push-button frame.",
      "**Do** keep game colour and motion for answer feedback."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** use Material You shapes: pill toggles, M3 chips, tonal FABs, large rounded cards. (Today's switches and Easy Days sliders are still Material and are the next to replace with XP checkboxes and trackbars.)",
      "**Don't** mix in another Windows era: no 98 grey bevels, Vista/7 glass, or 10/11 flat styling.",
      "**Don't** use soft blurred shadows or gradients outside the XP vocabulary above.",
      "**Don't** show Roboto where Tahoma can load.",
      "**Don't** let XP styling hide state: an active tab, a chosen option or a modified value must stay visible."
    ]
  }
}